From 33b8ba16652ba9d09c161e7721fcf41c552259e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 20:29:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] (be) ck-phdr-unwind libunwind native stack collector
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the stub collect step with the real libunwind walk: interrupt
each target thread with SIGRTMIN+6 queued via SI_QUEUE carrying a
per-request sequence token, seed libunwind from the saved ucontext
with UNW_INIT_SIGNAL_FRAME, walk via unw_step / unw_get_reg, then let
the shared run_collection resolve DSOs and report status. Defines
UNW_LOCAL_ONLY at the TU so the include resolves to the local-only
`_ULx86_64_*` symbols the linked libunwind archive exposes (the only
prefix it ships).

The slot ring + sequence + state machine mirror fp-walk so the safety
contract is the same: the handler validates si_pid + seq + slot state
before publishing, and a coordinator can only re-arm a slot in IDLE,
so a late handler in WALKING cannot poison the next dump. ck-phdr-
unwind needs no RBP-bounds or junk-RBP guard because libunwind walks
DWARF unwind info, not raw frame pointers.

A defense-in-depth `hasPHDRCache()` check refuses to signal if the
cache is missing — without it the handler's `unw_step` would call the
libc dl_iterate_phdr and take the loader lock, which is not async-
signal-safe. The cache is populated by the test runner's
updatePHDRCache() call before RUN_ALL_TESTS and by doris_main after
MemInfo::init (patch 2), so this is a guard, not the normal path.

Reference: <ck>/src/Storages/System/StorageSystemStackTrace.cpp;
<ck>/base/base/phdr_cache.cpp; <ck>/src/Common/StackTrace.cpp:470-498.
---
